WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.600
Marvel Studios surprised everyone with the
announcement that Avengers: Endgame is getting

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.580
a re-release just two months after the film
hit theaters.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.139
Marvel initially didn't say a whole lot about
the new version of Endgame, but now, the studio

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.900
has revealed what audiences will see up on
the big screen.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.190
In a press release rolled out on June 25th,
Marvel detailed that things will kick off

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.279
with a video introduction from Avengers: Endgame
co-director Anthony Russo.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.420
The film will then roll out just as it always
has, with no additional footage included.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.920
Things get exciting after the credits roll,
though, when an "unfinished deleted scene"

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:31.900
plays out.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.600
Marvel Studios didn't mention what happens
in the clip, but the folks at We Got This

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.360
Covered are claiming that it focuses on Mark
Ruffalo's Hulk.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.700
As of now, it's unclear what the big green
guy will get up to in this never-before-seen

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:46.500
sequence, but we'd love to see Bruce Banner
working in his lab to combine his brains with

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.360
the brawn of the Hulk.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.980
Similarly, Marvel didn't say anything in its
press release about a tribute, but we do know

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.000
that it's definitely coming, based on Feige's
past comments.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.760
MCU Cosmic reports that the tribute is an
homage to none other than Stan Lee, the longtime

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.960
creative leader of Marvel Comics who helped
create several of our favorite superheroes.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:09.100
Lee died at the age of 95 on November 12th,
2018, only a handful of months before the

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.050
theatrical debuts of Captain Marvel and Avengers:
Endgame.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.660
It's a mystery what exactly the tribute entails,
but it seems likely that the clip will touch

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.290
on Lee's incredible contributions to the world
of comics.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.340
Plus, it might even take a look back on the
many film cameos he made throughout the Marvel

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.420
Cinematic Universe.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.020
An unfinished, scrapped sequence that apparently
centers on Hulk definitely sounds intriguing,

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:32.530
but it may disappoint fans who were hoping
to finally see the scene featuring Katherine

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.720
Langford as a teenage Morgan Stark.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:39.340
The 13 Reasons Why actress was meant to appear
to Tony Stark in a vision after he uses the

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.030
Gauntlet and snaps his fingers.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.451
On an episode of the podcast Happy, Sad, Confused,
Joe Russo stated that Tony would have seen

00:01:45.451 --> 00:01:49.950
an older Morgan in the very same "metaphysical
way station" that Thanos went to after he

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.460
conducted his own snap in Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.380
"The intention was that his future daughter
— because these are the stones we're dealing

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.430
with, and they're magic — his future daughter
forgave him and sort of gave him peace to

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.420
go."

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:05.480
Right now, there's no way to know for sure
whether the deleted scene is all about Professor

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.880
Hulk or not, so there's a chance that this
scene could be the one shown during the Avengers:

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:09.899
Endgame re-release.

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:14.060
If it isn't, the older Morgan sequence could
be included the home release of the film.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:18.150
The final goodie tucked into the Avengers:
Endgame re-release that Marvel has confirmed

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.620
is a "special sneak peek" at the next MCU
movie, Spider-Man: Far From Home, due out

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.140
in theaters on July 2nd.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.310
Bringing Endgame back into theaters just days
before Far From Home opens is a risky move,

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.780
since fans could overlook the Spidey sequel
in favor of seeing Endgame again.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.480
Thankfully, it looks like Marvel is using
the re-release as a way to boost hype for

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.019
Peter Parker's second MCU solo outing.

00:02:39.019 --> 00:02:43.870
However, an introduction clip, a deleted scene,
a Spider-Man: Far From Home tease, and a tribute

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.989
montage may not be enough to attract viewers.

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:49.719
That could pose a problem since it appears
that Marvel's main reason for re-releasing

00:02:49.719 --> 00:02:53.859
Avengers: Endgame is to earn enough money
to beat out Avatar and become the biggest

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:54.920
movie of all time.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:03:00.019
At least those who do decide to give Endgame
another watch won't leave the cinema empty-handed;

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.040
re-release attendees will receive an exclusive
Avengers poster in select theaters while supplies

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:04.540
last.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.340
Catch the Avengers: Endgame re-release starting
on Friday, June 28th.

